 give me an outlet to express myself. It's like a little oasis of calm. Whenever I'm working on one, it's like I'm connecting back with myself. And yeah, the music helps too! Look at my garage, a little dirty, but everything is in its place.\n[Image caption: a photography of a garage with a bunch of tools hanging on the wall]\n[S25T13] (dia_id: D25:13)\n\nCalvin: Looking cool - what made you start working on cars?\n[S25T14] (dia_id: D25:14)\n\nDave: Ever since I was ten, I've been fascinated with how machines work. I found an old car in a neighbor's garage and asked if I could fix it. That's when my love for car engineering began! I enjoyed transforming it from broken-down to high-running, and that sense of accomplishment made me hooked—so I've been working on cars ever since.\n[Image caption: a photo of a man working on a car in a garage]\n[S25T15] (dia_id: D25:15)\n\nCalvin: Impressive! That must have taken a lot of skill and determination to bring that car back to life. Was it a classic car? Do you still have it or are you currently working on another project?\n[S25T16] (dia_id: D25:16)\n\nDave: Thanks Calvin! It was a fun project. I restored a car last year, but I sold it to a collector. Now I'm working on something new, and it's quite a challenge! Take a look at this wonderful car!\n[Image caption: a photo of a black car parked in a parking lot]\n[S25T17] (dia_id: D25:17)\n\nCalvin: Cool! Been wanting to try that. What would you say is the toughest part of car restoration?\n[S25T18] (dia_id: D25:18)\n\nDave: It takes a lot of patience, but the payoff is worth it. Paying extra attention to detail isn't easy, but it pays off.\n[S25T19] (dia_id: D25:19)\n\nCalvin: Yeah, details can really make a difference. It's what makes something great, like a well-crafted rap song or a sleek and stylish car.\n[S25T20] (dia_id: D25:20)\n\nDave: Yeah, for sure Calvin! Paying attention to details makes a big difference, whether it's in music or with vehicles. Little things can make a big impact!\n[S25T21] (dia_id: D25:21)\n\nCalvin: Yeah, Dave! Paying attention to those small details makes a difference. Without them, it's just average. As an artist, I want to create something extraordinary!\n[Image caption: a photo of a silver disc in a black frame on a table]\n[S25T22] (dia_id: D25:22)","text_sha256":"ca8534407b7cd3bc817f480ba54b6cae0d922f6dc9ea43320478da4a38f9da2b","timestamp":"2023-10-23T14:17:00"}],"integrity":{"post_tree_sha256":"ca39361e8e23f204a9fda55fc83e3ce7f411c7c8d582939aa63688c1923c7679","pre_tree_sha256":"ca39361e8e23f204a9fda55fc83e3ce7f411c7c8d582939aa63688c1923c7679","store_unchanged":true,"verified":true},"metrics":{"completion_tokens":510,"filesystem_tool_calls":0,"model_calls":4,"orchestration_calls":4,"prompt_tokens":8019,"provider_request_attempts":4,"provider_rounds":4,"token_usage_available":true,"total_tokens":8529},"model":{"requested_model":"x-test-2","served_models":["deepseek-v4.1-flash"]},"prompt_contract":{"derived_prompt_sha256":"6930d93099ac20b76e881b68cbb63b46e1a0a3e2ff43453db685551c3339a6dc","filesystem_tools_sha256":"98017e74a12c2eec4f0139c484d2d6bd809e4f37a8f96c7f419dc9591563dbfa","orchestration_actions_sha256":"3fa6b1160c2f7f9b2a8b3e232721d4ca78a161abb31af0d4f1f2e307b7354581","paper_prompt_id":"refind-appendix-a-stage1-plus-temporal-normalized-v1","paper_prompt_sha256":"20422063cc471ee1de75c38e4250e1a141a731ea2970786a6c715dc3c83cf7de"},"protocol_version":"shared-evidence-bundle-v1","question":{"conversation_id":"conv-50","question":"Would Dave prefer working on a Dodge Charger or a Subaru Forester?","question_id":"conv-50-q040","question_set_id":"locomo-conv50-main40-v1","run_position":28,"schema_version":1},"question_sha256":"53d25331330cc136a5b33312b96bdca40891d788df63095513d9c89d811e3a5f","runtime_contract":{"evidence_budget_limit":16000,"evidence_budget_unit":"characters","round_limit":4,"runtime_sha256":"ed611d544fa61c307748e870b8f9826deebb5bd1a3ab35b5ef999b6ad651ab17"},"schema_version":1,"search_ac